  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CHORCLIMA - Promoviendo la gesti&#xf3;n del conocimiento y buenas pr&#xe1;cticas al CC en Chiquimula, Guatemala</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In this proposal, ACDEBI will be institutionally strengthened through the development of internal policies, which will benefit 13 associates, including 3 associates belonging to the technical team, who will implement the various community projects.
It is expected to benefit at least 64 families (approximately 256 people) in 2 rural communities where the two climate stations will be implemented. As well as strengthening the technical team of ACDEBI and the community climate promoters.
MAIN OBJETIVE: Contribute to the institutional strengthening of ACDEBI, and promote a process of adaptation to Climate Change through Local Monitoring Systems, in order to guarantee Food Security and Sovereignty for communities of the Maya Chort&#xed; People.
Specific Objective: 1- To promote a process of construction of policies, manuals and codes, which guarantee the good action of ACDEBI&apos;s associates and technical team, NGOs, at the different levels of intervention. 2- Strengthen the resilience of indigenous families of the Maya Chort&#xed; people through the use of climate information (scientific and ancestral), which informs adaptation strategies in the face of climate change.</narrative>
  </description>
